  "result": "I found the bug, but I haven't changed any code yet because plan mode is on. I wrote the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-imperative-noodle.md`. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode because it isn't available in this session, so I can't submit the plan for approval.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/types.py:750-754`, `IntRange._clamp` returns `bound - dir`. When a value falls outside an open bound, the shared `convert` method passes `dir=1` below the minimum and `dir=-1` above the maximum. That `dir` means \"move inward\", so subtracting it moves the result outward.\n- `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returns `-1`. It should return `1`.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `9` returns `6`. It should return `4`.\n\nClosed bounds aren't affected, because `_clamp` returns the bound itself there.\n\n**Planned fix:** Change `bound - dir` to `bound + dir` in `IntRange._clamp`. `FloatRange` rejects clamping with open bounds, so it needs no change.\n\n**Tests:** I'd add open-bound clamp cases to `tests/test_types.py` and run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nIf you approve the plan or turn off plan mode, I'll make the change and run the tests.",
